{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1797","id":4174768775,"node_id":"PR_kwDOO5D6p8741eqH","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1797","diff_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1797.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1797.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/issues/1797","number":1797,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(kg): publish terminal Paper 5 reconciliation","user":{"login":"Samsen879","id":172257175,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkRvlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172257175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #1791\nParent: #1785\nPredecessor: #1790 / PR #1796\n\n## Outcome\n\nPublishes the bounded terminal Probability & Statistics 1 / Paper 5 semantic KG release from exact main `a1cca65feb82e74e6a416797c96cccc4717c2bff` (tree `498eb7cfeb053200f24dd36bfb8d68663b4d8f4f`). Current reviewed head is `e87e6c4e3bc3ddc8c73d92cc3d5992040ff5c87f` (tree `bbc09c0d87795d7275d15e9cc54374d79c24b31f`).\n\nNo sixth Family is created. All five #1786–#1790 ledger/delta pairs and the successor chain are raw-byte authenticated. Terminal construction now fails closed unless the active projection and structural authority match the exact path, SHA-256, and byte length pinned by the active P5-05 manifest, the P5-05 predecessor receipt matches that manifest, and the active inventory matches the admitted predecessor receipt. Rollback provenance remains bound to the unchanged active manifest.\n\n## Frozen terminal conservation\n\n- Historical papers: 72\n- Questions: 486 / 486\n- QuestionParts: 1,628 / 1,628\n- Score-owning / instruction-only: 1,231 / 397\n- Topics: 5 / 5\n- Question dispositions: 184 approved, 296 candidate, 6 rejected, 0 abstain\n- QuestionPart dispositions: 476 approved, 732 candidate, 23 rejected, 397 abstain\n- Epoch scope: 2016–2019 S1 Paper 6 components 61/62/63; 2020–2025 Paper 5 components 51/52/53/55\n- Old Mechanics 2 / post-2020 Statistics 2 admitted: 0 / 0\n- Historical matching bundles: 491 = 486 active + 5 authenticated safe out-of-scope rejections; unexplained difference 0\n\n## Exact 10-part evidence reconciliation\n\nEvery changed part retains exact QP/MS references and old-to-new provenance.\n\nThe four-part predecessor gap `qrow_9709_m20_qp_52_q02` is resolved at existing structural owners after directly opening both QP and all three MS crops:\n\n- `q02`: unenriched -> abstain; instruction-only; explicitly `mixed_family_instruction_root_unowned` with null Family ownership\n- `q02/a`: unenriched -> approved; P5-03 Probability combined/geometric sum\n- `q02/b`: unenriched -> approved; P5-04 discrete distribution\n- `q02/c`: unenriched -> approved; P5-04 expectation\n\nTwo physically exact P5-01 foreign-Family rejections are reclaimed after reopening every listed original crop:\n\n- `qrow_9709_w25_qp_53_q04::q04/a`: rejected -> approved; P5-04 distribution\n- `...::q04/b`: rejected -> approved; P5-04 variance\n- `...::q04/c`: rejected -> approved; P5-03 complement core plus one geometric alternative\n- `qrow_9709_w25_qp_55_q06::q06/a`: rejected -> approved; P5-05 normal probability\n- `...::q06/b`: rejected -> approved; P5-05 normal parameter inference\n- `...::q06/c`: rejected -> approved; P5-05 normal approximation with continuity correction\n\nFor `w25/53/Q4c`, `alternative_procedure_model_refs` contains only the actual `evaluate_combined_events` alternative PI. `apply_probability_complement` remains primary. Both branches have independent steps 1..3 with no duplicate PM/PI.\n\n## Semantic and visual readback\n\n- QuestionTypes: 53, counting distinct primary plus secondary types across all status boundaries\n- ProcedureModels / ProcedureInstances / ProcedureStepInstances: 52 / 569 / 1,233\n- Approved ProcedureInstances / approved ProcedureModels / reuse ratio: 538 / 50 / 10.76\n- Supporting ProcedureInstances / alternative branches: 93 / 30\n- Candidate-only ProcedureModels: `fit_normal_distribution_model`, `normalise_counted_outcomes`\n- Active authenticated bundles: 486\n- Visually reviewed Questions / QuestionParts: 486 / 1,628\n- Unique QP / MS / total images: 736 / 1,101 / 1,837\n- Independently decoded images: 1,837\n- Missing, unreadable, or mismatched: 0\n- Visual/layout approved / candidate-plus-abstain: 476 / 1,129\n- Text-only approvals: 0\n- Visual-review minutes: unavailable in predecessor authority and intentionally not invented\n- Terminal cache build/hit/miss: 0 / 0 / 0\n- Inherited active P5-05 cache build/hit/miss: 1 / 1 / 1\n- Bounded artifacts: 8\n- Four non-self-referential terminal data payloads: 13,593,874 bytes\n\nThe independent terminal image validator checks PNG signature, chunk bounds and CRCs, IHDR/color/depth, zlib decode, exact scanline lengths, and row filters after SHA authentication. A hash-matching corrupt-image negative test fails closed as unreadable. It shares no producer/runtime validator implementation.\n\n## Release artifacts\n\n- reconciliation delta: `1c9c829c2a7d49a89d1ec6a3bc9489cd20f29e784eac8f77ca9f5ea6350e8242`\n- terminal projection: `857417356cc267cb9019b53fad69b159eb2f689b00e8d61d49fe11186fabe24a`\n- disposition ledger: `05c7bf68930d041e9dc12cbdf3e5ee5fc59f157879caee11fcaf3491bb1e5ad5`\n- epoch-scope ledger: `667aabcd892488bbb779cdf2cc993c714787019d33029dde87b1190a0791bb99`\n- readback: `1079634f8a9b6feb7ee6de6027ec3ead6c809b340d46456ea914d235380f9d31`\n- rollback target: `88ec5c3853ba08e33df6ac0a53e8fbf210a79d16858bbd8c67b3cb67b71b9abb`\n- visual ledger: `65a3d92d03d3e7c3a9179a14c0a0dfdd2439636622113c208715d813a6ce7911`\n- terminal manifest: `913bcb84a24601ff608f2ddb1d666666591ffa1d008bc6c3ce71c0bcf1eed0a7`\n\nTerminal sequence 6 binds the exact active P5-05 manifest and terminal receipts. Rollback sequence 7 points exactly to the active P5-05 manifest. Deterministic active/terminal/rollback replay passes.\n\n## Gates and verification\n\nPASS with zero: approved score parts without MS review, approved visual parts without QP review, text-only approvals, candidate exposure, primary ownership conflicts, duplicate active identities, duplicate cross-Family ProcedureModels, dangling edges, structural orphans, unsupported inferred edges, stale taxonomy/image/predecessor refs, graph copies, historical byte changes, future predecessor mutation, validator implementation sharing, and remote writes.\n\n- Five P5-01…P5-05 direct checks: deterministic rebuild PASS and physical corpus authentication PASS\n- Family tests: 15 + 16 + 18 + 12 + 12 = 73 PASS\n- P5-06 focused tests: 12 PASS, including active-authority drift and corrupt-image negative cases\n- Future producer / harness: 30 / 27 PASS\n- Total: 142 PASS\n- Terminal check: deterministic rebuild and active/terminal/rollback replay PASS\n- `npm run lint:changed`, Python compile, AST independence, duplicate-JSON-key, and diff checks: PASS\n\n## Scope boundary\n\nAdds only eight bounded terminal JSON artifacts, one builder, and one focused test. No global structural graph or P1/P3/P4 directory is copied. No Paper 6, frontend, RAG, Supabase, or production integration is included.\n\nAll five substantive automated review threads on the original head were fixed generically, regression tested, replied to, and resolved on this same PR. Fresh exact-head independent review remains required before merge. Do not merge or close the parent chain from this implementation handoff.","created_at":"2026-07-31T03:20:35Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T04:07:50Z","closed_at":"2026-07-31T04:01:00Z","merged_at":"2026-07-31T04:01:00Z","merge_commit_sha":"51df66abaa8844e66e4c6a79436e3057cda917fc","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1797/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1797/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/issues/1797/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/statuses/e87e6c4e3bc3ddc8c73d92cc3d5992040ff5c87f","head":{"label":"Samsen879:task/1791-p5-06-terminal-reconciliation","ref":"task/1791-p5-06-terminal-reconciliation","sha":"e87e6c4e3bc3ddc8c73d92cc3d5992040ff5c87f","user":{"login":"Samsen879","id":172257175,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkRvlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172257175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/repos","ev